content.text:
verdict: clean
scenario_results:
  - {scenario: 1, result: pass, notes: "Self-definition (four parts + tests) precedes the first principle; every principle carries exactly the four parts; all cross-references use backticked slugs, and the opening routes unknown slugs to the working set."}
  - {scenario: 2, result: pass, notes: "Each statement decides work alone; decision terms resolve to the statement, the opening's taxonomies (lead shop/BC-shop, product/operational contract), or the named glossary terms; a few bullets carry paired keywords but each clause is independently decidable — noted as stumbles, not fails."}
  - {scenario: 3, result: pass, notes: "Every rationale shows a generic failure; citations are all well-known published sources (Parnas, Hyrum's law, Evans, NIST RBAC, reflexion models, IEEE 29148); no product operational history appears."}
  - {scenario: 4, result: pass, notes: "Every implication names its actor (creators, maintainers, architects, contract authors, reviewers, integrators, process authors, designers, refactorers) and traces to a statement clause; one implication per bullet throughout."}
  - {scenario: 5, result: pass, notes: "Six columns match the six principles; all five opening tests have rows (plus two clearly-labeled extra rows); every claimed pass was reproducible on this read."}
  - {scenario: 6, result: pass, notes: "Each principle rejects real work (internals-as-documentation, out-of-band coupling, per-actor rulebooks, whole-system reads, code-as-authority, untracked backlogs), and each opposite is one honest shops commonly run."}
  - {scenario: mechanical, result: pass, notes: "Capitalized MUST/SHOULD/MAY appear only in statements and in the opening's explicitly permitted mentions; no normative keyword leaks into rationales, implications, or the screen."}
stumbles: ["Each Bounded Context MUST be contained and produced by exactly one BC-shop; the lead shop MUST NOT contain one. — two keywords in one bullet, though the second clause is already entailed by the opening's lead-shop definition", "The design — descriptions, contracts, recorded decisions — MUST be the authoritative statement of what the product is and does, and code MUST conform to it. — two MUSTs joined by 'and'; decidable, but the closest thing in the set to a fused sentence", "forward — every design element MUST have code implementing it (did we build what we said?) — and reverse — every code element MUST be called for by the design — three MUSTs nested in one bullet's em-dash structure", "the role performing it — 'role' is load-bearing in actor-neutral-discipline but is neither in the opening's glossary list nor defined in the opening; the actor-kind clause rescues the decision", "maintained as an artifact — 'artifact' is undefined and read generically"]
top_changes: ["Split bidirectional-conformance's both-directions bullet so forward and reverse are each their own obligation bullet (they are independently checkable checks sharing one bullet)", "Add 'role' to the opening's defined-terms pointer or define it alongside the shop taxonomy", "Drop the lead-shop clause from knowable-shape's containment bullet, or move it to the opening's taxonomy where the fact already lives"]
